00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:51.689
Vancouver City Council has unanimously told staff to fund shelters and seats at 100

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:56.089
trans-linked stops that have neither, and to have them in by September 2027.

00:03:56.789 --> 00:04:01.509
Daily Hive covered Wednesday's meeting, November 18th, when an amended motion from co-op

00:04:01.509 --> 00:04:06.089
councillor Sean Orr passed, and council cleared all 11 member motions on the agenda.

00:04:06.089 --> 00:04:11.769
The first hundred locations go into the 2027 budget, generally the busier suitable stops.

00:04:12.229 --> 00:04:18.309
Staff also have to report by April 2027 on covering every stop where a shelter and bench can physically fit,

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:22.329
with a target of December 2029, or cast it as access.

00:04:22.869 --> 00:04:28.949
Someone with a disability, or a senior who has trouble moving, should not have to stand in the rain just to get through the day, he said,

00:04:29.189 --> 00:04:31.449
and he argued the amenities raise ridership.

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:35.089
He credited Cope colleague Solomon Yeekirin with leading the draft.

00:04:35.549 --> 00:04:39.609
The two estimate only about half of Vancouver stops already have a shelter with a bench.

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:46.409
Shelter expansion was a Cope campaign promise, and Yeekirin has treated transit fixes as a core priority in office.

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:53.649
He said he knows the half-hour weight in the rain for the number 3, the number 8, or the number 49, with no bench and no cover,

00:04:54.029 --> 00:04:57.889
and that rain more than 40% of the year makes a bare half of stops unacceptable.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:02.749
Translink looks after shelters on its own land, including off-street exchanges.

00:05:03.249 --> 00:05:06.609
On the sidewalk, Metro cities generally install and maintain them.

00:05:07.189 --> 00:05:11.689
Mayor Pete Frye asked for a fuller account of the cleaning, safety, and access work, and

00:05:11.689 --> 00:05:12.829
