The case on both sides of a mountain pleasant hotel rezoning

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:10.890
is now in front of the new council, Daily High Reports.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.510
Yesterday that council was already taking up

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:15.390
reversals of the last term's decisions.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:19.510
On Wednesday, co-op councillor Solomon Yeekirin and Chloe Leslie

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:23.950
asked whether the same reach covers the hotel development policy and a rezoning that

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.310
is approved only in principle.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:30.330
Michael Cook, chair of the Myron Manor Collective and a member of the Vancouver Tenants Union,

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:35.550
asked for previously approved hotel bylaws and rezonings to be repealed, especially his

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:37.290
building, and sent back to staff.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:42.910
Myron Manor, at 75 East Eighth Avenue, is a three-story rental with more than two dozen

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.650
units beside the future Mount Pleasant Sky train station.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:50.790
On July 28th, after a hearing spread over three dates, the previous council approved

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:57.050
in principle a 21-story tower with 190 hotel units and two floors of industrial space,

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:00.070
from Lotus Capital Corporation and Nicola Real Estate.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.110
Cook's reason is that rental homes should not become hotels.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:09.670
He wants subsection 3.2.2.1D, replaced with a binding rule that no rental apartments in

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:14.370
the city are replaced by hotels, plus a city fund so tenant groups can buy buildings and

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.730
and turn them into co-ops or community land trusts.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:23.230
The policy passed in April 2025, and last amended in May, 2026, is how the city pursues

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.850
a net 10,000 hotel rooms over the coming decades.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:31.130
The city and destination Vancouver say those rooms support tourism, jobs, and big events.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:36.190
Destination Vancouver says the shortage shows up in occupancy and overnight rates, and

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:41.110
that Vancouver has fewer hotel rooms than in the early 2000s, even after short-term rentals

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:41.690
were restricted.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:46.390
Staff have said the room goal is on track if you count the pipeline, while many projects

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.190
are still proposals and approved ones may never be built.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.670
Mixing hotels with rental or strata housing, they say, has also made some new housing financially

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.270
possible.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:12:00.690
Unite here local 40, which represents many hotel workers, has opposed several proposals

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.650
and policies, and has gone to court.

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:08.910
In July 2026 hearings, then ABC counselors accused the union and its supporters of filibustering.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:13.170
staff told this council that adding cooks requests to a tenant rights motion

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:17.810
would greatly widen the work, that repealing a rezoning is possible but very complex

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:22.170
and that council can also refuse to enact a by-law after an in-principle vote.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.730
They said a later briefing would cover the policy in that subsection.

